1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
[English subtitles are available]

2
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:08,310
[A long time ago,]

3
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:11,960
[there was a huge flood.]

4
00:00:12,050 --> 00:00:16,010
[It washed away
the humans' lies and deceits,]

5
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:19,970
[evils and wars.]

6
00:00:20,060 --> 00:00:23,230
[A lot of life was taken.]

7
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:25,820
[When the flood came,]

8
00:00:25,910 --> 00:00:29,830
[two brothers happened
to be fishing out at sea.]

9
00:00:29,910 --> 00:00:31,760
[When they got home,]

10
00:00:31,850 --> 00:00:36,510
[they found that the village
had been submerged.]

11
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:40,740
[The older brother tried to cheer
his younger brother up.]

12
00:00:40,870 --> 00:00:42,320
[He said to him,]

13
00:00:42,410 --> 00:00:44,610
["Far, far away,]

14
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:49,190
[there is a big tree on Mount Kalalayan.]

15
00:00:49,270 --> 00:00:54,950
[The big tree is so tall that it seems
to pierce through the sky of Kakarayan.]

16
00:00:55,080 --> 00:01:00,710
[Its roots hold the ground firmly,]

17
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:06,300
[while its leaves create
an impenetrable canopy]

18
00:01:06,430 --> 00:01:11,400
[that can stop any storm."]

19
00:01:12,110 --> 00:01:17,700
[So the two brothers set out
in order to live.]

20
00:01:17,780 --> 00:01:24,470
[They saved many people along the way.]

21
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:26,800
[In their small fishing boats,]

22
00:01:26,890 --> 00:01:30,240
[they traveled in search of a tree]

23
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:36,310
[that perched on Mount Kalalayan.]

24
00:01:36,660 --> 00:01:39,700
[The more people came on board,]

25
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:43,000
[the more the older brother felt guilty.]

26
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:48,940
[Only when they saw
the legendary 10,000-year-old tree]

27
00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:53,560
[did he finally feel at ease.]

28
00:01:53,640 --> 00:01:57,160
[He confessed to the survivors]

29
00:01:57,250 --> 00:02:02,000
[that the huge, old tree]

30
00:02:02,090 --> 00:02:05,740
[was a story he made up
to deceive his brother.]

31
00:02:05,830 --> 00:02:09,620
[Unexpectedly, the tree started
to wither instantly.]

32
00:02:09,699 --> 00:02:13,140
[As his lie got exposed,]

33
00:02:13,270 --> 00:02:16,480
[the tree vanished into the deluge.]

34
00:02:20,220 --> 00:02:23,079
♫ The blue sky, the wind blows ♫

35
00:02:23,690 --> 00:02:26,690
♫ Like your tenderness ♫

36
00:02:24,750 --> 00:02:29,810
[On the day of the last rainfall,
the Kawas return to their homeland]

37
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:32,450
♫ You leave behind the outlines of fate ♫

38
00:02:34,829 --> 00:02:37,470
♫ I'm waiting for the day ♫

39
00:02:37,420 --> 00:02:38,740
Thank you.

40
00:02:38,350 --> 00:02:40,770
♫ When the rain falls
after a long drought ♫

41
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:42,000
♫ Will you ♫

42
00:02:42,090 --> 00:02:46,930
♫ Remember what I said to you ♫

43
00:02:48,860 --> 00:03:03,160
♫ Take away my everything
and let me be your everything ♫

44
00:03:03,470 --> 00:03:19,440
♫ Take away my everything
and let me be your everything ♫

45
00:03:45,090 --> 00:03:46,280
Your name?

46
00:03:46,370 --> 00:03:47,560
Palang.

47
00:03:48,130 --> 00:03:51,340
Share the blessings.

48
00:03:54,510 --> 00:03:56,970
Next, please.

49
00:03:57,850 --> 00:03:59,079
Your name?

50
00:03:59,170 --> 00:04:00,320
Hafay.

51
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:02,960
He is Hafay from Taitung.

52
00:04:03,040 --> 00:04:05,380
The god of millet.

53
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:10,480
Share the blessings.

54
00:04:19,279 --> 00:04:20,600
Thank you, everyone.

55
00:04:23,770 --> 00:04:26,010
Fali, I have an update.

56
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:27,680
Evacuation Echelon 27

57
00:04:27,770 --> 00:04:29,220
has taken all the Kawas

58
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:30,370
from this world.

59
00:04:30,460 --> 00:04:31,820
That's good.

60
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:33,980
What about you?

61
00:04:34,110 --> 00:04:35,870
When are you and your husband evacuating?

62
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:39,650
I have some matters
at the Cause and Effect Correction Bureau.

63
00:04:39,740 --> 00:04:40,440
I will bring him

64
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:42,120
to the final extraction point
within the given time

65
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:44,140
and leave together with the messenger.

66
00:05:21,450 --> 00:05:23,690
Excuse me. Make way, please.

67
00:05:25,150 --> 00:05:26,250
Senior.

68
00:05:26,330 --> 00:05:28,010
Where's the victim?

69
00:05:28,670 --> 00:05:30,070
She was just here.

70
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:32,320
I told you to keep watch.
Find out where she went.

71
00:05:42,700 --> 00:05:44,290
[Li Pu-hui.]

72
00:05:44,370 --> 00:05:45,430
As the god of wisdom,

73
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:47,850
can you please
have a little bit of wisdom yourself?

74
00:05:47,940 --> 00:05:50,090
Can you please stop being so ridiculous?

75
00:05:50,180 --> 00:05:51,330
Don't try to be smart

76
00:05:51,409 --> 00:05:52,510
and use these little tricks, okay?

77
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:54,490
Can you think about the consequences
before you do something?

78
00:05:54,620 --> 00:05:55,940
Also, I really don't want to nag you.

79
00:05:56,030 --> 00:05:57,920
But you're driving me crazy.

80
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:06,680
Answer me, Li Pu-hui.

81
00:06:06,770 --> 00:06:08,480
Do you know if 'Orad...

82
00:06:09,060 --> 00:06:12,710
Bye, honey! I'll miss you!

83
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:15,000
Stop nagging!

84
00:06:15,080 --> 00:06:17,810
A big heart for you!

85
00:06:21,640 --> 00:06:22,780
Fali.

86
00:06:24,150 --> 00:06:25,860
I know it's time to evacuate,

87
00:06:25,950 --> 00:06:27,100
but give me some time.

88
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:28,020
I'll get him.

89
00:06:28,150 --> 00:06:29,160
Don't bother.

90
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:31,760
Go back to Pinokayan.

91
00:06:32,290 --> 00:06:34,750
Leave the matter
of the god of wisdom to me.

92
00:06:35,540 --> 00:06:37,170
I was the one who let him get away.

93
00:06:37,260 --> 00:06:38,760
I can't trouble you with that.

94
00:06:38,840 --> 00:06:40,520
I'll catch him no matter what.

95
00:06:52,440 --> 00:06:53,630
You go ahead.

96
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:56,440
I'll take care of the rest.

97
00:06:57,500 --> 00:07:00,140
[Dongli]

98
00:07:01,940 --> 00:07:09,950
[Episode 8, Behind Every Lie
is a Wish Waiting to Come True]

99
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:41,120
Let me explain.

100
00:08:41,250 --> 00:08:42,440
Due to your health condition,

101
00:08:42,520 --> 00:08:44,460
we have planned the trip

102
00:08:44,590 --> 00:08:46,000
to be more relaxing

103
00:08:46,090 --> 00:08:47,940
and you won't need to exhaust yourself.

104
00:08:48,020 --> 00:08:49,870
For example, we can go to a museum,

105
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:50,840
maybe take part

106
00:08:50,930 --> 00:08:53,080
in making homemade jam,
or other similar activities.

107
00:08:53,170 --> 00:08:55,500
[I'm sorry to say this.]

108
00:08:55,640 --> 00:08:57,260
Lu Sung-en, whom you've just met,

109
00:08:57,350 --> 00:08:58,630
will die of a heart attack

110
00:08:58,720 --> 00:09:01,440
in the near future.

111
00:09:01,580 --> 00:09:02,810
The original order of cause and effect

112
00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:04,740
wasn't supposed to be like this.

113
00:09:04,880 --> 00:09:06,020
Because...

114
00:09:06,110 --> 00:09:08,620
in the original plan of Kakarayan,

115
00:09:08,750 --> 00:09:10,680
she gets a heart transplant surgery

116
00:09:10,770 --> 00:09:12,270
and becomes healthy again.

117
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:14,600
She gets to live out her life.

118
00:09:16,010 --> 00:09:18,300
But it all changed

119
00:09:18,430 --> 00:09:20,360
because of one person.

120
00:09:22,430 --> 00:09:24,320
We can go to an art gallery after drawing.

121
00:09:24,410 --> 00:09:24,760
What do you think?

122
00:09:24,900 --> 00:09:25,560
Okay.

123
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:27,050
Also,

124
00:09:27,140 --> 00:09:29,600
Mr. Sung's foundation
has already given me a heads-up.

125
00:09:29,730 --> 00:09:31,850
They want the sites and hotels
to be as close to a medical...

126
00:09:31,930 --> 00:09:32,680
So...

127
00:09:32,770 --> 00:09:35,230
if I have some questions,
can I voice them out?

128
00:09:35,850 --> 00:09:36,950
Of course.

129
00:09:37,040 --> 00:09:38,310
As Mr. Sung's client,

130
00:09:38,400 --> 00:09:39,410
you're also my client.

131
00:09:39,550 --> 00:09:41,610
Your requests come first.

132
00:09:41,750 --> 00:09:43,510
In this part that I read, it says

133
00:09:43,590 --> 00:09:45,310
that you've arranged the first dinner

134
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:47,470
at an all-you-can-eat buffet at the hotel.

135
00:09:47,550 --> 00:09:49,450
Can you make it simpler?

136
00:09:49,530 --> 00:09:52,390
I don't eat much. This will be a waste.

137
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:53,140
And...

138
00:09:53,230 --> 00:09:55,740
when I look at the distance
between the attractions,

139
00:09:55,830 --> 00:09:56,880
it's not that far.

140
00:09:56,970 --> 00:09:59,260
I think we'll be able to get there
if we walk a bit.

141
00:09:59,350 --> 00:10:01,110
Maybe we can rent a bike

142
00:10:01,190 --> 00:10:02,600
and ride there.

143
00:10:02,690 --> 00:10:05,680
I don't think
we need to rent another tour bus.

144
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:09,600
Sung-en, let me explain.

145
00:10:10,350 --> 00:10:12,330
You've been in the hospital for so long.

146
00:10:12,410 --> 00:10:13,650
This will be your first trip

147
00:10:13,730 --> 00:10:15,190
in a long while, right?

148
00:10:15,670 --> 00:10:17,740
So don't worry

149
00:10:17,830 --> 00:10:18,750
about a little thing like money.

150
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:21,520
You can relax and be yourself.

151
00:10:21,650 --> 00:10:23,550
That's what traveling is all about.

152
00:10:23,630 --> 00:10:25,570
It's not about the money.

153
00:10:27,240 --> 00:10:30,320
I don't want my first trip

154
00:10:30,410 --> 00:10:32,350
to only make myself happy

155
00:10:32,430 --> 00:10:34,770
but cause a burden to the surrounding.

156
00:10:34,850 --> 00:10:37,980
So you're saying...

157
00:10:38,110 --> 00:10:40,400
you wish to go
on a more eco-friendly trip?

158
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:41,980
Yes, that's right.

159
00:10:42,110 --> 00:10:43,210
An eco-friendly trip

160
00:10:43,340 --> 00:10:45,240
isn't as complicated as you imagined.

161
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:46,730
Make a little change every day.

162
00:10:46,820 --> 00:10:49,020
Soon enough,
it will make a big difference.

163
00:10:49,110 --> 00:10:51,260
I don't think
being environmentally-conscious

164
00:10:51,350 --> 00:10:53,200
is about going out of our way.

165
00:10:53,290 --> 00:10:55,400
It should start from our daily lives.

166
00:10:55,490 --> 00:10:56,680
That's how we can save the Earth.

167
00:10:57,340 --> 00:10:59,050
What do you think, Tien-ti?

168
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:04,860
I think Sung-en is right.

169
00:11:05,340 --> 00:11:08,030
Let's do as she wants.

170
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:09,920
That's great. Here.

171
00:11:10,930 --> 00:11:12,740
Be careful.

172
00:11:13,310 --> 00:11:14,410
Let's move on to the next one.

173
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:15,240
Okay.

174
00:11:16,260 --> 00:11:19,560
You'll be attending a painting workshop.

175
00:11:19,640 --> 00:11:20,390
Do you like it?

176
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:21,490
Yes.

177
00:11:21,580 --> 00:11:24,180
[Mountain Travel]

178
00:11:31,480 --> 00:11:33,200
In my opinion,

179
00:11:33,330 --> 00:11:35,000
it's not that you want
to change your fate.

180
00:11:35,130 --> 00:11:36,760
In fact,

181
00:11:37,820 --> 00:11:40,500
you just want to live

182
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:44,500
at the expense of someone else's future.

183
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:49,830
You mean that if I die,

184
00:11:51,590 --> 00:11:53,650
the girl can live?

185
00:11:53,740 --> 00:11:55,190
You don't have to act

186
00:11:55,280 --> 00:11:57,090
as if you're making a sacrifice for her.

187
00:11:58,630 --> 00:12:00,030
You're not that great.

188
00:12:00,780 --> 00:12:03,160
You're just returning something
that doesn't belong to you

189
00:12:03,290 --> 00:12:04,650
back to its owner.

190
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:26,170
Thank you.

191
00:12:29,560 --> 00:12:32,990
You two are acting weird.

192
00:12:35,450 --> 00:12:36,690
You two have been acting strange

193
00:12:36,820 --> 00:12:38,840
since we came back from the hospital.

194
00:12:38,930 --> 00:12:40,870
Is it because of the chat you had

195
00:12:40,950 --> 00:12:42,230
with Mr. Sung when he left?

196
00:12:42,410 --> 00:12:43,460
What chat?

197
00:12:46,100 --> 00:12:48,790
Could it be that Mr. Sung found out

198
00:12:48,870 --> 00:12:50,680
that you two are secretly dating

199
00:12:50,770 --> 00:12:51,910
and asked you to break up

200
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:53,760
or not to keep in touch again?

201
00:12:53,850 --> 00:12:55,470
What are you talking about, Wu Yi-han?

202
00:12:55,610 --> 00:12:57,450
What's in that head of yours?

203
00:13:01,100 --> 00:13:03,350
I was talking to Mr. Sung

204
00:13:03,660 --> 00:13:04,800
about the budget.

205
00:13:05,590 --> 00:13:06,340
Really?

206
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:07,750
Yes, that was all.

207
00:13:09,110 --> 00:13:10,260
Okay.

208
00:13:10,340 --> 00:13:11,360
If you're free now,

209
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:12,540
can you take a look

210
00:13:12,630 --> 00:13:14,520
at the updated itinerary for Sung-en?

211
00:13:14,660 --> 00:13:15,930
Is there anything else
that needs to be fixed?

212
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:18,090
Leave it here. I'll read it later.

213
00:13:18,220 --> 00:13:19,940
No, do it now.

214
00:13:20,110 --> 00:13:22,000
It won't take long.

215
00:13:22,140 --> 00:13:23,590
Quickly, come on.

216
00:13:27,110 --> 00:13:27,680
Here.

217
00:13:33,930 --> 00:13:36,570
[Itinerary]

218
00:13:41,100 --> 00:13:42,240
Is it okay?

219
00:13:47,220 --> 00:13:48,320
Wu Yi-han.

220
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:49,590
You're really trying hard

221
00:13:49,680 --> 00:13:52,100
to get Mr. Sung's attention.

222
00:13:52,720 --> 00:13:54,780
I advise you to give it up.

223
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:57,380
I've never seen you so motivated

224
00:13:57,470 --> 00:13:59,230
and dedicated about a job before.

225
00:14:01,780 --> 00:14:03,450
Okay, I admit it.

226
00:14:03,980 --> 00:14:05,740
It's true that I started this

227
00:14:05,830 --> 00:14:07,940
to get Mr. Sung's attention.

228
00:14:08,030 --> 00:14:09,740
That was why I worked hard.

229
00:14:10,540 --> 00:14:11,850
But now,

230
00:14:11,990 --> 00:14:14,140
I'm devoted and serious about this trip

231
00:14:14,230 --> 00:14:15,770
because I really want to help Sung-en

232
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:16,830
in some way.

233
00:14:18,190 --> 00:14:20,790
You want to help Sung-en in some way?

234
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:23,870
It's true.

235
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:24,920
Today, when I heard

236
00:14:25,010 --> 00:14:28,000
what she said at the hospital,

237
00:14:28,130 --> 00:14:30,420
I thought the little girl
was so pretentious.

238
00:14:30,510 --> 00:14:31,740
A young kid

239
00:14:31,870 --> 00:14:35,220
preaching about wanting to save the Earth.

240
00:14:35,880 --> 00:14:37,510
But I was like, "Forget it."

241
00:14:37,640 --> 00:14:38,610
I should do my research

242
00:14:38,690 --> 00:14:40,540
and plan
some eco-friendly activities for her.

243
00:14:41,510 --> 00:14:42,960
Then...

244
00:14:43,050 --> 00:14:44,720
do you know what I found?

245
00:14:45,250 --> 00:14:46,170
What?

246
00:14:47,050 --> 00:14:49,910
She's not an ordinary high school student.

247
00:14:50,490 --> 00:14:54,450
She is "Greenie from the Next Class."

248
00:14:55,020 --> 00:14:58,010
Three, two, one.

249
00:14:58,100 --> 00:14:58,980
Okay.

250
00:14:59,640 --> 00:15:01,790
Twenty-four hours
without air conditioning.

251
00:15:01,880 --> 00:15:03,330
Challenge completed.

252
00:15:04,390 --> 00:15:06,370
[Twenty-four hours
without air conditioning.]

253
00:15:06,500 --> 00:15:08,260
[This is what I thought.]

254
00:15:08,530 --> 00:15:11,520
[Humans are weaker than I thought.]

255
00:15:12,440 --> 00:15:14,690
[Just like when I started the challenge]

256
00:15:14,770 --> 00:15:16,490
[at noon yesterday,]

257
00:15:16,580 --> 00:15:17,990
[I remember the temperature]

258
00:15:18,070 --> 00:15:20,190
[was 33.5 degrees Celsius.]

259
00:15:20,270 --> 00:15:22,120
[It was hot,]

260
00:15:22,250 --> 00:15:24,190
[but it was still bearable.]

261
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:26,960
[But look at the temperature now.]

262
00:15:27,090 --> 00:15:29,120
[It's 35 degrees Celsius.]

263
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:30,790
[It's one and a half degrees higher,]

264
00:15:30,880 --> 00:15:33,080
[but it feels like a different world.]

265
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:35,410
[I thought I was going to die
from the heat.]

266
00:15:34,750 --> 00:15:35,800
[A High Schooler's Eco-friendly Diary]

267
00:15:35,500 --> 00:15:36,730
Greenie From the Next Class

268
00:15:35,890 --> 00:15:39,190
[No electricity for 24 hours.]

269
00:15:36,820 --> 00:15:38,050
is a green-centric community

270
00:15:38,140 --> 00:15:40,340
run by high school students.

271
00:15:39,280 --> 00:15:42,490
[Marine environmental protection
and community care]

272
00:15:40,420 --> 00:15:43,720
High school students
from all over Taiwan

273
00:15:42,580 --> 00:15:43,900
[Ocean environment protection
and sustainability]

274
00:15:43,810 --> 00:15:46,280
shoot fun and interesting vlogs

275
00:15:46,410 --> 00:15:48,390
to encourage a more
environmentally conscious lifestyle

276
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:50,190
through everyday living.

277
00:15:50,980 --> 00:15:52,960
And the founder of this community

278
00:15:53,140 --> 00:15:54,860
is none other than Lu Sung-en.

279
00:15:56,750 --> 00:15:58,110
I thought she was just a girl

280
00:15:58,200 --> 00:16:00,360
that talked about going green.

281
00:16:00,970 --> 00:16:03,960
I didn't expect
that she actually walked the talk.

282
00:16:04,050 --> 00:16:05,720
She even led many other people

283
00:16:05,810 --> 00:16:08,010
to join her on this mission.

284
00:16:08,100 --> 00:16:10,700
God is so unfair.

285
00:16:10,780 --> 00:16:12,100
If she had a healthy body

286
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:14,220
like the rest of us,

287
00:16:14,300 --> 00:16:17,960
perhaps she could have done more.

288
00:16:19,140 --> 00:16:20,600
This world

289
00:16:20,680 --> 00:16:22,620
might become better.

290
00:16:24,820 --> 00:16:28,340
[It's said that if the Earth's temperature
rises by six degrees Celsius,]

291
00:16:28,430 --> 00:16:30,320
[humanity will start to go extinct.]

292
00:16:30,450 --> 00:16:32,120
[But after humans disappear,]

293
00:16:32,210 --> 00:16:34,150
[the earth will still exist.]

294
00:16:34,230 --> 00:16:35,950
[So from this information,]

295
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:38,550
[the environmental protection
we've been advocating]

296
00:16:38,630 --> 00:16:40,000
[isn't teaching us]

297
00:16:40,090 --> 00:16:41,800
[how to protect the environment.]

298
00:16:41,930 --> 00:16:42,860
[On the contrary,]

299
00:16:42,950 --> 00:16:45,890
[the environment
has always protected us humans.]

300
00:16:45,980 --> 00:16:48,800
[So the real aim of conservation]

301
00:16:48,930 --> 00:16:51,260
[is not to save the environment,
but the people.]

302
00:16:51,350 --> 00:16:52,760
[Let's make a little change]

303
00:16:52,850 --> 00:16:54,520
[every single day.]

304
00:16:54,610 --> 00:16:55,620
[When it's put together,]

305
00:16:55,710 --> 00:16:58,300
[it will be the revolution
that changes the world.]

306
00:17:00,550 --> 00:17:01,690
[Dear Greenies.]

307
00:17:01,780 --> 00:17:03,360
[Let's save humanity]

308
00:17:03,490 --> 00:17:04,680
[through our everyday lives!]

309
00:17:04,770 --> 00:17:06,089
[Go!]

310
00:17:57,040 --> 00:17:58,270
Good morning.

311
00:17:58,930 --> 00:18:00,470
Did you sleep well?

312
00:18:02,060 --> 00:18:02,850
It was okay.

313
00:18:04,780 --> 00:18:06,190
Are you still thinking about yesterday?

314
00:18:06,280 --> 00:18:08,220
I have a lot to do later.

315
00:18:08,300 --> 00:18:10,060
I'm going to get ready to leave.

316
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:24,230
[I'll give you another chance.]

317
00:18:24,320 --> 00:18:27,750
Remove all her memories of you.

318
00:18:27,840 --> 00:18:30,480
Do it according to the Reflection of Time
that Kakarayan has given you.

319
00:18:30,610 --> 00:18:32,500
You have to make Hsieh Tien-ti

320
00:18:32,590 --> 00:18:34,750
go back to where she belongs.

321
00:18:42,620 --> 00:18:44,250
[Pu, have you taken the photos?]

322
00:18:44,380 --> 00:18:45,000
Yes.

323
00:18:45,090 --> 00:18:48,830
Okay, great.
The reception desk looks okay. Next is...

324
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:50,060
This is a good spot.
Can you take one for me?

325
00:18:50,190 --> 00:18:50,850
Okay.

326
00:18:50,940 --> 00:18:53,230
-One, two, three.
-Peace.

327
00:18:53,360 --> 00:18:54,550
Okay.

328
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:56,970
The reception desk and hotel look okay.

329
00:18:57,050 --> 00:18:59,340
Bicycle...

330
00:19:00,710 --> 00:19:02,070
I think I saw a bike rental service

331
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:03,830
at the reception desk.

332
00:19:03,920 --> 00:19:04,890
Let's look into it later.

333
00:19:04,970 --> 00:19:05,810
Okay.

334
00:19:06,470 --> 00:19:08,140
With Sung-en's current condition,

335
00:19:08,230 --> 00:19:10,470
is it really okay to ride a bike?

336
00:19:10,560 --> 00:19:12,540
I was thinking the same thing.

337
00:19:12,630 --> 00:19:15,930
If it's too hot or rainy in the afternoon,

338
00:19:16,020 --> 00:19:18,440
I don't know if her body can take it.

339
00:19:19,100 --> 00:19:19,890
Tien-ti.

340
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:26,050
Hsieh Tien-ti, are you all right?

341
00:19:27,110 --> 00:19:29,660
You've been zoning out the whole day.

342
00:19:29,750 --> 00:19:30,670
It's a good thing I'm here.

343
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:32,780
Otherwise, this job would be screwed.

344
00:19:33,710 --> 00:19:36,260
Sorry, I didn't sleep well last night.

345
00:19:37,140 --> 00:19:38,550
I'll go check on Sung-en's room.

346
00:19:38,630 --> 00:19:39,510
I'll be right back.

347
00:19:39,600 --> 00:19:40,040
Okay.

348
00:19:40,170 --> 00:19:41,100
Okay!

349
00:19:41,190 --> 00:19:42,770
I'm here, so don't worry.

350
00:19:43,520 --> 00:19:45,190
Let's look around the restaurant.

351
00:19:45,280 --> 00:19:45,630
Come one.

352
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:46,600
Let's go.

353
00:19:51,130 --> 00:19:52,050
Tien-ti.

354
00:19:55,570 --> 00:19:56,450
Why are you here?

355
00:20:01,730 --> 00:20:02,570
Are you okay?

356
00:20:05,300 --> 00:20:05,960
I'm fine.

357
00:20:07,670 --> 00:20:09,340
I'll take a look at Sung-en's room first.

358
00:20:12,380 --> 00:20:15,900
I hope you won't take
what you heard yesterday

359
00:20:15,990 --> 00:20:17,840
to heart.

360
00:20:18,410 --> 00:20:21,620
Whether or not Sung-en lives

361
00:20:21,710 --> 00:20:23,420
has nothing to do with you.

362
00:20:25,620 --> 00:20:26,940
Don't feel guilty.

363
00:20:32,090 --> 00:20:33,900
How can it have nothing to do with me?

364
00:20:37,060 --> 00:20:37,810
Because of me...

365
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:40,670
I told you, it has nothing to do with you.

366
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:43,050
I'm the one who decided to let you live.

367
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:45,470
Naturally, I should be the one

368
00:20:46,390 --> 00:20:47,620
to handle the repercussions.

369
00:21:12,660 --> 00:21:14,240
From now on,

370
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:18,730
you won't remember what you heard

371
00:21:19,130 --> 00:21:20,970
about Sung-en yesterday.

372
00:21:22,870 --> 00:21:24,800
You'll forget about the car accident.

373
00:21:25,590 --> 00:21:26,960
You'll forget me

374
00:21:28,850 --> 00:21:32,720
and everything about the Kawas.

375
00:21:34,750 --> 00:21:36,240
So from now on,

376
00:21:37,300 --> 00:21:39,630
no matter how messed up the world gets,

377
00:21:40,330 --> 00:21:41,790
all you have to do

378
00:21:42,580 --> 00:21:44,250
is to take care of yourself.

379
00:21:45,310 --> 00:21:48,470
Live your life

380
00:21:48,560 --> 00:21:50,410
to the fullest.

381
00:22:01,810 --> 00:22:02,910
And then?

382
00:22:03,960 --> 00:22:06,380
What are you going to do next?

383
00:22:12,850 --> 00:22:14,260
You're no longer the messenger.

384
00:22:14,350 --> 00:22:15,970
You're not even a Kawas.

385
00:22:16,110 --> 00:22:18,310
You're in no position
to negotiate with Fali.

386
00:22:21,650 --> 00:22:23,010
If you think a useless trick

387
00:22:23,100 --> 00:22:24,110
like trading your life

388
00:22:24,250 --> 00:22:26,450
to persuade Fali to spare Hsieh Tien-ti,

389
00:22:26,580 --> 00:22:28,290
you're too naive.

390
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:31,020
Because even if Fali grants your request,

391
00:22:32,520 --> 00:22:34,100
I won't leave her alone either.

392
00:22:38,410 --> 00:22:39,950
But then again,

393
00:22:40,040 --> 00:22:40,740
I wouldn't be able to see

394
00:22:40,830 --> 00:22:42,770
this angry look on your face.

395
00:22:42,900 --> 00:22:44,440
It wouldn't be fun at all.

396
00:22:45,230 --> 00:22:46,200
I'll hold on

397
00:22:46,290 --> 00:22:47,830
to this comb for you.

398
00:23:08,240 --> 00:23:09,520
Leave that woman to me.

399
00:23:09,650 --> 00:23:10,310
You just have to do

400
00:23:10,400 --> 00:23:12,780
what you promised me.

401
00:23:19,510 --> 00:23:20,780
'Orad.

402
00:23:23,070 --> 00:23:24,350
What are you doing?

403
00:23:29,140 --> 00:23:30,110
I came to see you.

404
00:23:34,640 --> 00:23:35,610
If you want to ask me

405
00:23:35,740 --> 00:23:38,120
about yesterday,

406
00:23:38,250 --> 00:23:40,540
can we leave that to later?

407
00:23:41,590 --> 00:23:45,380
My mind is kind of blank right now.

408
00:23:48,150 --> 00:23:50,090
I'll go check on Sung-en's room first.

409
00:24:51,420 --> 00:24:52,340
You got it wrong.

410
00:24:56,570 --> 00:24:58,200
[Be careful.]

411
00:24:58,280 --> 00:25:00,040
[If you accidentally kill this human,]

412
00:25:00,130 --> 00:25:01,280
[you'll end up like me,]

413
00:25:01,360 --> 00:25:03,430
[falling from grace]

414
00:25:03,560 --> 00:25:06,160
[and turning into your most hated Kariah.]

415
00:25:10,210 --> 00:25:11,480
Not so fast.

416
00:25:11,570 --> 00:25:13,240
I'll take you somewhere.

417
00:25:19,800 --> 00:25:21,960
Right now, you're in my heart.

418
00:25:22,040 --> 00:25:23,060
This is a scene

419
00:25:23,140 --> 00:25:25,210
I've seen before.

420
00:25:29,960 --> 00:25:31,200
Don't forget.

421
00:25:31,280 --> 00:25:32,820
I'm the goddess of cloud

422
00:25:32,910 --> 00:25:35,020
who can freely travel
through a person's heart.

423
00:25:35,110 --> 00:25:36,170
Unless I allow it,

424
00:25:36,300 --> 00:25:37,710
no one can catch me.

425
00:25:38,370 --> 00:25:40,220
I followed you back
to the Cause and Effect Correction Bureau

426
00:25:40,300 --> 00:25:41,050
because I wanted to know

427
00:25:41,140 --> 00:25:42,900
what exactly you were planning.

428
00:25:43,210 --> 00:25:44,530
But the more I observe you,

429
00:25:44,620 --> 00:25:46,680
the more questions I have.

430
00:25:47,120 --> 00:25:49,680
What did you do to all the Kawas?

431
00:25:50,120 --> 00:25:51,740
What's behind that door?

432
00:25:52,670 --> 00:25:54,780
Why did you send all the Kawas away

433
00:25:54,870 --> 00:25:57,290
but stayed behind alone?

434
00:26:02,390 --> 00:26:03,270
If all of this

435
00:26:03,360 --> 00:26:05,600
is to correct the faulty cause and effect,

436
00:26:05,690 --> 00:26:06,970
why don't you just get rid

437
00:26:07,050 --> 00:26:09,080
of Hsieh Tien-ti yourself

438
00:26:09,170 --> 00:26:11,810
rather than getting 'Orad to deal with it?

439
00:26:11,940 --> 00:26:12,730
I find it odd.

440
00:26:12,820 --> 00:26:14,580
Stop beating around the bush.

441
00:26:14,670 --> 00:26:15,590
Go ahead.

442
00:26:16,650 --> 00:26:18,890
Tell me what you know.

443
00:26:20,300 --> 00:26:21,400
You're scared.

444
00:26:22,540 --> 00:26:25,180
You're afraid that 'Orad
didn't just lose his powers,

445
00:26:25,310 --> 00:26:26,410
but that Kakarayan

446
00:26:26,550 --> 00:26:28,350
has actually dismissed him
as the messenger.

447
00:26:28,480 --> 00:26:29,490
So you keep using

448
00:26:29,630 --> 00:26:31,390
Hsieh Tien-ti to test 'Orad

449
00:26:31,470 --> 00:26:34,070
to check if Kakarayan has really returned.

450
00:26:34,160 --> 00:26:35,960
Because as Kakarayan's secret keeper,

451
00:26:36,090 --> 00:26:37,680
you've betrayed him.

452
00:26:39,750 --> 00:26:42,030
[What a shame.]

453
00:26:42,170 --> 00:26:44,230
That was so close.

454
00:26:44,320 --> 00:26:46,610
If you really kill this human,

455
00:26:47,490 --> 00:26:49,510
we'll be on the same team.

456
00:27:08,960 --> 00:27:10,770
We've made some changes to the itinerary.

457
00:27:10,850 --> 00:27:13,010
I came today to brief you.

458
00:27:14,900 --> 00:27:17,670
The other lady didn't come today?

459
00:27:17,800 --> 00:27:19,390
She's funny.

460
00:27:20,220 --> 00:27:21,900
You mean Wu Yi-han?

461
00:27:21,980 --> 00:27:24,140
She's busy at work today.

462
00:27:24,760 --> 00:27:26,600
I know she's loud. Did she scare you?

463
00:27:26,690 --> 00:27:28,190
No, she's funny.

464
00:27:28,280 --> 00:27:29,550
We had a great time.

465
00:27:29,640 --> 00:27:30,960
Okay.

466
00:27:31,050 --> 00:27:34,040
She's very serious about this project.

467
00:27:34,130 --> 00:27:37,030
We've been to some lodgings

468
00:27:37,120 --> 00:27:38,220
and places to visit.

469
00:27:38,310 --> 00:27:40,330
We organized the information.

470
00:27:40,460 --> 00:27:41,430
Take a look.

471
00:27:41,520 --> 00:27:42,440
Thank you.

472
00:27:46,450 --> 00:27:48,690
[Your own customized three-day travel
package of carbon emission reduction]

473
00:27:48,300 --> 00:27:49,920
We saw your videos.

474
00:27:50,010 --> 00:27:50,940
You said

475
00:27:51,070 --> 00:27:53,580
that if we made small changes every day,

476
00:27:53,660 --> 00:27:56,570
the world would be different.

477
00:27:56,660 --> 00:27:59,210
So I figured I shouldn't print copies

478
00:27:59,300 --> 00:28:00,700
but should show it to you
on the laptop instead.

479
00:28:01,580 --> 00:28:02,820
Thank you.

480
00:28:03,170 --> 00:28:05,590
I didn't expect you to watch my videos.

481
00:28:05,680 --> 00:28:08,010
My videos haven't been updated
in a long time.

482
00:28:12,360 --> 00:28:14,430
You really went cycling.

483
00:28:14,520 --> 00:28:15,220
Yes.

484
00:28:15,360 --> 00:28:17,380
The weather is nice, it looks hot.

485
00:28:17,470 --> 00:28:19,800
Yes, it was so hot that day.
She was sweating so much.

486
00:28:19,930 --> 00:28:21,250
I told her to tie her hair up,
but she refused.

487
00:28:21,340 --> 00:28:23,050
She wanted to look pretty.

488
00:28:24,200 --> 00:28:25,430
Can I ask you something, miss?

489
00:28:25,520 --> 00:28:27,370
How long have you been
growing your hair out?

490
00:28:28,820 --> 00:28:30,970
You really went cycling.

491
00:28:31,060 --> 00:28:32,650
Yes, it was so hot that day.

492
00:28:32,780 --> 00:28:34,490
She was sweating so much.

493
00:28:34,580 --> 00:28:37,000
I told her to tie her hair up,
but she refused.

494
00:28:37,090 --> 00:28:38,280
She wanted to look pretty.

495
00:28:38,370 --> 00:28:39,730
Can I ask you something, miss?

496
00:28:39,820 --> 00:28:41,620
How long have you been
growing your hair out?

497
00:28:42,590 --> 00:28:44,440
Miss, did I ask something

498
00:28:44,530 --> 00:28:46,240
I shouldn't have asked?

499
00:28:46,330 --> 00:28:47,650
No.

500
00:28:49,060 --> 00:28:50,990
I was just thinking
about how to answer you.

501
00:28:54,600 --> 00:28:56,710
My hair grows really fast.

502
00:28:56,800 --> 00:28:58,170
It probably took me

503
00:28:58,300 --> 00:29:00,100
two years. I didn't keep track.

504
00:29:01,070 --> 00:29:02,520
I think your hair is nice.

505
00:29:02,610 --> 00:29:04,370
I want the same hairstyle as yours.

506
00:29:04,770 --> 00:29:05,950
Really?

507
00:29:06,830 --> 00:29:07,760
I agree.

508
00:29:07,850 --> 00:29:09,830
If you grow your hair longer,

509
00:29:09,910 --> 00:29:11,060
it will look very pretty.

510
00:29:11,150 --> 00:29:13,870
Really? I think so too.

511
00:29:13,960 --> 00:29:16,250
But my mom wouldn't let me grow it out.

512
00:29:16,340 --> 00:29:18,230
Is it because you're sick?

513
00:29:18,360 --> 00:29:19,420
Yes.

514
00:29:19,510 --> 00:29:21,880
I've undergone a lot of operations.

515
00:29:21,970 --> 00:29:23,600
And each time,

516
00:29:23,690 --> 00:29:25,310
it was always without notice.

517
00:29:25,400 --> 00:29:27,600
That's why my mom cut my hair short.

518
00:29:27,730 --> 00:29:29,450
It will be more convenient

519
00:29:29,540 --> 00:29:30,950
if anything happens.

520
00:29:31,030 --> 00:29:32,050
So I've had my hair short

521
00:29:32,130 --> 00:29:33,800
for a long time.

522
00:29:37,810 --> 00:29:39,220
Make way!

523
00:29:40,800 --> 00:29:42,080
Has the family been notified?

524
00:29:42,160 --> 00:29:43,750
Yes, we've notified them.

525
00:29:59,590 --> 00:30:00,420
Sung-en.

526
00:30:02,230 --> 00:30:04,780
I know you're looking forward
to this trip.

527
00:30:06,670 --> 00:30:08,300
But have you thought

528
00:30:08,390 --> 00:30:11,470
perhaps we could postpone it?

529
00:30:14,460 --> 00:30:15,300
Why?

530
00:30:17,800 --> 00:30:18,820
To be honest,

531
00:30:18,900 --> 00:30:20,750
we simplified the itinerary

532
00:30:20,880 --> 00:30:22,950
as best as we could.

533
00:30:23,040 --> 00:30:24,670
But now,

534
00:30:24,760 --> 00:30:26,910
as long as you're out and about,

535
00:30:27,790 --> 00:30:29,460
there's still a risk.

536
00:30:30,300 --> 00:30:31,440
Your mom told me

537
00:30:31,530 --> 00:30:33,690
that you fainted not long ago.

538
00:30:35,270 --> 00:30:36,990
So I thought

539
00:30:37,080 --> 00:30:39,410
instead of taking risks like this

540
00:30:39,720 --> 00:30:42,180
and not being able to fully enjoy it,

541
00:30:43,240 --> 00:30:45,740
let's wait for you to get better

542
00:30:45,830 --> 00:30:47,410
in the future.

543
00:30:47,500 --> 00:30:49,790
We can go somewhere a little bit further

544
00:30:49,880 --> 00:30:51,900
and have a real trip.

545
00:30:54,320 --> 00:30:56,700
Did my mom tell you to persuade me?

546
00:30:57,490 --> 00:31:00,440
Or does your company
find it too bothersome?

547
00:31:02,460 --> 00:31:04,350
No.

548
00:31:05,370 --> 00:31:07,170
This is what I think.

549
00:31:07,920 --> 00:31:10,030
The tourist sites will always be there.

550
00:31:10,160 --> 00:31:12,540
When you're better in the future,

551
00:31:12,930 --> 00:31:14,120
we can go there

552
00:31:14,210 --> 00:31:15,660
anytime you want.

553
00:31:16,720 --> 00:31:19,270
Do you know which word I heard

554
00:31:19,840 --> 00:31:21,730
and hated the most

555
00:31:22,390 --> 00:31:24,590
after I became sick?

556
00:31:27,370 --> 00:31:29,130
It's the word "future."

557
00:31:30,270 --> 00:31:32,380
No matter what I want to do,

558
00:31:32,470 --> 00:31:34,270
everyone tells me,

559
00:31:34,360 --> 00:31:36,960
"You can do that

560
00:31:37,090 --> 00:31:38,590
when you're better in the future.

561
00:31:39,070 --> 00:31:40,700
There's no rush

562
00:31:42,630 --> 00:31:44,170
because you'll have a lot of time
in the future

563
00:31:44,260 --> 00:31:45,450
to do them

564
00:31:45,800 --> 00:31:47,520
and you can go to many places."

565
00:31:48,220 --> 00:31:49,450
But the people

566
00:31:49,540 --> 00:31:51,260
who kept talking about the future to me

567
00:31:51,830 --> 00:31:53,150
had never thought about this.

568
00:31:53,460 --> 00:31:55,000
With my body like this,

569
00:31:55,700 --> 00:31:58,340
even if I get a surgery
and become healthy again,

570
00:31:59,090 --> 00:32:01,200
I can't live to over 40 years old.

571
00:32:01,860 --> 00:32:03,270
I don't have much time.

572
00:32:03,580 --> 00:32:06,220
I might not even wake up
the next time I sleep.

573
00:32:06,520 --> 00:32:08,500
Yet I have to be tied to the "future"

574
00:32:08,590 --> 00:32:10,040
you people speak of.

575
00:32:10,130 --> 00:32:11,450
I can't do anything

576
00:32:11,540 --> 00:32:13,210
nor go anywhere.

577
00:32:16,600 --> 00:32:20,470
Miss, I know you're worried.

578
00:32:20,560 --> 00:32:22,410
It's normal.

579
00:32:22,500 --> 00:32:24,080
But you must know this.

580
00:32:24,170 --> 00:32:26,590
I really want to see the ocean.

581
00:32:26,680 --> 00:32:29,100
I want to hear the sound of the mountains.

582
00:32:29,930 --> 00:32:31,650
I don't want

583
00:32:32,130 --> 00:32:34,420
to only tell people through the screen

584
00:32:34,550 --> 00:32:36,880
to make the world a better place.

585
00:32:36,970 --> 00:32:39,220
But in actual fact, I don't even know

586
00:32:39,300 --> 00:32:41,460
how the real world looks like.

587
00:32:43,880 --> 00:32:46,210
Why are all of you taking away my future?

588
00:32:53,960 --> 00:32:55,940
I'm sorry. Please excuse me.

589
00:33:19,120 --> 00:33:21,370
What should I do?

590
00:33:25,190 --> 00:33:26,470
I know

591
00:33:26,560 --> 00:33:29,020
what will become of Sung-en.

592
00:33:30,870 --> 00:33:32,500
But I don't dare to tell her.

593
00:33:35,800 --> 00:33:37,950
Because of my...

594
00:33:38,090 --> 00:33:39,410
It's not your fault.

595
00:33:40,860 --> 00:33:42,490
The more I get to know Sung-en,

596
00:33:42,570 --> 00:33:44,910
the more I'm beginning to understand

597
00:33:46,180 --> 00:33:49,530
why Kakarayan
made the arrangement that way.

598
00:33:50,930 --> 00:33:52,560
What do you mean?

599
00:33:52,650 --> 00:33:54,670
Sung-en is not like me.

600
00:33:56,130 --> 00:33:58,590
No matter what her future holds,

601
00:33:59,600 --> 00:34:01,850
she truly believes

602
00:34:02,070 --> 00:34:04,130
that her existence can help this world

603
00:34:04,220 --> 00:34:05,810
change for the better.

604
00:34:07,650 --> 00:34:08,889
Unlike me.

605
00:34:10,780 --> 00:34:12,050
I always thought

606
00:34:12,190 --> 00:34:13,290
whether or not I existed,

607
00:34:13,370 --> 00:34:15,090
it wouldn't make any difference.

608
00:34:17,199 --> 00:34:19,400
So for the world,

609
00:34:20,060 --> 00:34:22,219
the one who should live

610
00:34:22,300 --> 00:34:24,150
is her and not me.

611
00:34:27,449 --> 00:34:29,260
Maybe right from the start,

612
00:34:30,620 --> 00:34:32,030
I shouldn't have tried to change

613
00:34:32,120 --> 00:34:34,010
the Reflection of Time you saw

614
00:34:34,100 --> 00:34:35,770
about my death.

615
00:34:36,340 --> 00:34:36,909
Maybe I should've done

616
00:34:37,040 --> 00:34:39,730
what Fali had told me to do.

617
00:34:40,780 --> 00:34:42,810
This life belongs to her.

618
00:34:44,440 --> 00:34:45,980
I should give it back to her.

619
00:34:46,860 --> 00:34:48,179
Stop it.

620
00:34:49,980 --> 00:34:51,170
It's not your fault.

621
00:34:52,800 --> 00:34:54,159
Ms. Tien-ti.

622
00:34:58,430 --> 00:35:02,170
You forgot your bags.

623
00:35:20,780 --> 00:35:22,060
Sung-en.

624
00:35:22,450 --> 00:35:23,730
Sung-en.

625
00:35:34,550 --> 00:35:36,790
It's not that you want
to change your fate.

626
00:35:36,880 --> 00:35:38,470
In fact,

627
00:35:39,040 --> 00:35:41,810
you just want to live

628
00:35:43,310 --> 00:35:45,860
at the expense of someone else's future.

629
00:35:46,870 --> 00:35:48,890
Make way!

630
00:35:50,350 --> 00:35:51,620
Has the family been notified?

631
00:35:51,750 --> 00:35:53,510
Yes, we've notified them.

632
00:36:33,030 --> 00:36:40,280
[Operation room]

633
00:36:48,070 --> 00:36:54,190
[Please insert your health insurance card]

634
00:36:56,390 --> 00:36:58,460
Dr. Hsieh, is Sung-en...

635
00:36:58,590 --> 00:37:00,390
How is our Sung-en?

636
00:37:00,520 --> 00:37:02,990
I'm sorry, but the surgery didn't go well.

637
00:37:03,080 --> 00:37:04,790
We can only rely on an ECMO machine

638
00:37:04,880 --> 00:37:06,600
to keep Sung-en alive.

639
00:37:06,730 --> 00:37:07,390
We will monitor

640
00:37:07,480 --> 00:37:09,100
her condition for the time being

641
00:37:09,540 --> 00:37:11,480
before we decide on the next move.

642
00:37:11,570 --> 00:37:12,930
We have to ask you to be prepared

643
00:37:13,020 --> 00:37:15,700
for the worst-case scenario.

644
00:37:34,670 --> 00:37:36,120
You should go home.

645
00:37:36,210 --> 00:37:37,440
I'm going to the office

646
00:37:37,530 --> 00:37:39,290
to inform Yi-han and the rest

647
00:37:40,610 --> 00:37:42,540
about halting Sung-en's trip.

648
00:37:43,730 --> 00:37:44,570
Tien-ti.

649
00:37:46,330 --> 00:37:47,600
Do you know why

650
00:37:48,180 --> 00:37:49,630
there is no "sorry"

651
00:37:49,710 --> 00:37:50,770
in the language of the Kawas?

652
00:37:53,720 --> 00:37:55,430
It's because we don't regret.

653
00:37:56,360 --> 00:37:59,530
We know that feeling regret

654
00:37:59,610 --> 00:38:02,520
won't undo what has happened.

655
00:38:04,850 --> 00:38:07,010
That's why I want you to know.

656
00:38:08,150 --> 00:38:10,350
No matter how upset you are,

657
00:38:11,630 --> 00:38:13,650
it's just unnecessary feelings.

658
00:38:14,090 --> 00:38:16,950
So even though
I'm beating myself up over it,

659
00:38:17,830 --> 00:38:20,340
you think it's just unnecessary feelings?

660
00:38:21,260 --> 00:38:23,950
Yes, it's all unnecessary.

661
00:38:30,240 --> 00:38:31,510
I'm a human.

662
00:38:32,750 --> 00:38:34,290
I'm not a Kawas.

663
00:38:35,520 --> 00:38:37,450
Can you stop telling me these things?

664
00:38:38,070 --> 00:38:39,480
Kawas like you,

665
00:38:40,710 --> 00:38:41,460
who always just stood by

666
00:38:41,590 --> 00:38:43,090
and watched what happened

667
00:38:43,170 --> 00:38:44,540
will never know

668
00:38:44,630 --> 00:38:46,080
how painful it is for us

669
00:38:46,170 --> 00:38:47,840
who are living through it.
